An :IF whose whole condition is a negation and that has its own :ELSE
fires diag.negative_logic (info, on the negation token): .NOT. x, !x and
.NOT. (a .AND. b) all qualify. The :ELSE of the nested :IF inside the
first block belongs to the inner block, not the outer one.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Route;
	:PARAMETERS bReady, bUrgent, bLocal;
	:DECLARE sQueue;
	:IF .NOT. bReady;
		sQueue := "hold";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := "run";
	:ENDIF;
	:IF !bUrgent;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-normal";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-urgent";
	:ENDIF;
	:IF .NOT. (bUrgent .AND. bLocal);
		sQueue := sQueue + "-remote";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-local";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sQueue;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Route;
	:PARAMETERS bReady, bUrgent, bLocal;
	:DECLARE sQueue;
	:IF .NOT. bReady;
		sQueue := "hold";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := "run";
	:ENDIF;

	:IF !bUrgent;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-normal";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-urgent";
	:ENDIF;

	:IF .NOT. (bUrgent .AND. bLocal);
		sQueue := sQueue + "-remote";
	:ELSE;
		sQueue := sQueue + "-local";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sQueue;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:6-4:11 info negative_logic: Consider inverting this condition to use positive logic: swap the :IF and :ELSE branches and remove the negation.
9:6-9:7 info negative_logic: Consider inverting this condition to use positive logic: swap the :IF and :ELSE branches and remove the negation.
14:6-14:11 info negative_logic: Consider inverting this condition to use positive logic: swap the :IF and :ELSE branches and remove the negation.
